sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: Completed-only publication sequence
  accDescr: A caller runtime commits all 26 ordered stages, including the terminal analytics payload, before explicit finalization. StockResearchAgents stages the strict CompanyAnalyticsResultV1 with its exact submission and seven authoritative artifacts, while the lifecycle retains a separate control ID and exposes the canonical result ID through result_run_id. The viewer remains empty until required publication state is ready.

  participant H as Caller runtime
  participant P as StockResearchAgents core
  participant S as Durable storage
  participant Q as Quality outcome index
  participant M as Decision memory (optional)
  participant V as Dossier Viewer

  H->>P: Prepare company-analytics.v1 request
  P-->>H: 26-stage workflow + run-control.v1
  loop Each of 26 ordered stages
    H->>P: Opaque completed-stage envelope
    P->>S: Persist revision + bounded output references
    V-->>P: Query completed result
    P-->>V: No completed dossier
  end
  H->>P: Finalize CompanyAnalyticsSubmissionV1
  P->>P: Validate outer analytics and embedded CompanyResearchSubmissionV1 / ResearchDossierV1
  alt Rejected or incomplete
    P-->>H: Typed validation failure
    P-->>V: No completed dossier
  else Accepted
    P->>P: Derive canonical result ID and retain lifecycle ID separately
    P->>S: Stage CompanyAnalyticsResultV1 + canonical events
    P->>Q: Stage hidden derived index
    P->>M: Stage decision memory when enabled
    P->>Q: Publish index, or reconstruct after recovery
    Q-->>P: Quality publication acknowledged
    P->>S: Atomic canonical result publication
    S-->>P: Completed publication receipt
    P->>M: Publish staged decision memory when enabled
    M-->>P: Memory ready or disabled
    P-->>H: control.result_run_id = canonical result ID
    V->>P: Query canonical completed result
    P-->>V: Read-only RunView
  end

  Note over S,Q: Reader gate waits for result quality and enabled memory readiness through recoverable coordination
